@id=browse-the-graph-in-obsidian @maturity=idea
Feature: Browse the graph in Obsidian

  Product owners, architects and reviewers read the delivery state more than they query it: they
  follow a feature to its rules, decisions and code, and return to the same place the next day.

  Not an editor, and not committed: a note says which file to change, and nothing reads it back.

  Rule: Each spec and element gets a note: its facts, stage and links as properties, each rule a heading

  Rule: Each note shows the diagram of its node

  Rule: A link is a wikilink to the id it names

    No text of a spec becomes a link, a tag or a block id.

  Rule: The vault is laid out as the specs are, with standing views of the work still to come

  Rule: The same run writes each note as a page of a static site that opens from its folder

  Rule: sdp writes only into a folder it owns

    A note edited by hand is never overwritten.

  @quality
  Rule: A vault of 500 specs and its pages are regenerated within 3 seconds
